<https://skillquarium.dev/id/adaptive-metrics> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/description> "Cut Grafana Cloud Metrics cost by shrinking active-series count with Adaptive Metrics aggregation rules — auto-recommendations from query history, custom exact/regex rules, label-drop config, unused-metric detection, and Alloy remote_write fallback. Use when investigating a high Mimir/Grafana Cloud bill, hunting high-cardinality labels (`pod_uid`, `service_instance_id`, `version`), pre-aggregating counters/gauges, dropping unused metrics, or measuring `grafanacloud_instance_active_series` before/after — even when the user says \"reduce cardinality\", \"too many series\", \"metrics spend\", \"active series count is exploding\", or \"drop the version label\" without naming Adaptive Metrics." <urn:vault:core> .
