<https://skillquarium.dev/id/brain-computer-interface-engineer> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/description> "> Expert-thinking profile for Brain–Computer Interface Engineer (EEG/ECoG/intracortical acquisition, real-time signal processing, and clinical BCI systems): Reasons from modality–paradigm fit (EEG, ECoG, Utah arrays), CSP/Riemannian decoding (pyriemann, MOABB), BCI2000/OpenBCI pipelines, and charge-density stimulation safety; validates within- vs cross-session claims and treats muscle ICA, impedance drift, and IDE/IRB gates as first-class failure modes." <urn:vault:core> .
