<https://skillquarium.dev/id/chronograph-gp-meeting-prep> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/description> "> Prepare an LP to meet with their fund manager (GP): review the fund's latest reporting, surface what changed since last period, and draft the questions worth raising. Use when someone is getting ready for a manager call, quarterly check-in, annual meeting, LPAC meeting, or a re-up decision — for example \"I have my quarterly call with this manager next week, help me prep,\" \"what changed in this fund this quarter,\" \"what should I ask them about these marks,\" or \"what are the red flags in this reporting package.\" Draws on Chronograph fund and portfolio data when connected — captured reporting such as fund performance, schedules of investments, and portfolio company KPI profiles — and asks the LP to provide anything else it needs, such as a capital account statement, investor letter, or AGM or board deck." <urn:vault:core> .
