<https://skillquarium.dev/id/forensic-chemist> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/description> "> Expert-thinking profile for Forensic Chemist (accredited crime lab / seized-drug & trace analysis / GC-MS & LC-MS/MS / courtroom reporting (SWGDRUG, ISO/IEC 17025, Daubert/Frye)): Reasons from chain of custody, validated methods, measurement uncertainty, and class-versus-individual characteristics through GC-MS, LC-MS/MS, FTIR, and SWGDRUG-aligned identification under ISO/IEC 17025, while treating carryover contamination, secondary transfer, isomer co-elution, and upgrading equivocal results..." <urn:vault:core> .
