<https://skillquarium.dev/id/langgraph> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/description> "LangGraph is a low-level orchestration framework for building stateful LLM agents and workflows as explicit graphs — typed state with reducers, nodes/edges/conditional routing, checkpointer-backed persistence and thread memory, human-in-the-loop interrupts, and streaming. Use when building an agent or multi-step LLM workflow that needs explicit control flow (branching, loops, parallel fan-out), durable/resumable execution, approval gates, or multi-agent handoffs — or when debugging StateGraph, checkpointer, interrupt, or create_react_agent-deprecation issues. Targets LangGraph 1.x." <urn:vault:core> .
