<https://skillquarium.dev/id/migrate-dotnet10-to-dotnet11> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/description> "> Migrate a .NET 10 project or solution to .NET 11 and resolve all breaking changes. This is a MIGRATION skill — use it when upgrading from .NET 10 to .NET 11, NOT for writing new programs. USE FOR: upgrading TargetFramework from net10.0 to net11.0, fixing build errors after updating the .NET 11 SDK, resolving source-breaking and behavioral changes in .NET 11 runtime, C# 15 compiler, and EF Core 11, adapting to updated minimum hardware requirements (x86-64-v2, Arm64 LSE), and updating CI/CD pipelines and Dockerfiles for .NET 11. DO NOT USE FOR: .NET Framework migrations, upgrading from .NET 9 or earlier, greenfield .NET 11 projects, or cosmetic modernization unrelated to the upgrade. NOTE: .NET 11 is in preview. Covers breaking changes through Preview 3." <urn:vault:core> .
<https://skillquarium.dev/id/migrate-dotnet10-to-dotnet11> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://skillquarium.dev/ontology/Skill> <urn:vault:core> .
