<https://skillquarium.dev/id/ngs-cli-toolkit> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/description> "The core command-line NGS workhorses for going from raw reads to variants — bwa-mem2/minimap2/bowtie2 (alignment), samtools (BAM sort/index/stats/view), bcftools (VCF call/filter/normalize/query), GATK4 (BQSR, HaplotypeCaller, best practices), and plink2 (genotype QC, PCA, GWAS). Use for read alignment, BAM/CRAM manipulation, variant calling and VCF wrangling on the command line. For Python-native BAM/VCF access use pysam; for full managed pipelines use the nf-core wrappers." <urn:vault:core> .
