<https://skillquarium.dev/id/nvmolkit-usage> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/description> ">- Write code that calls the installed nvMolKit Python API for GPU-accelerated, batched RDKit-style operations - Morgan fingerprints, Tanimoto/cosine similarity, ETKDG conformer embedding, MMFF/UFF optimization, TFD, conformer RMSD, Butina clustering, and substructure search. Use when the user is importing `nvmolkit.*`, debugging an `nvmolkit` call, choosing between nvMolKit and RDKit for a batched cheminformatics workflow, or wiring nvMolKit results into a torch/numpy pipeline. Out of scope: building nvMolKit from source." <urn:vault:core> .
