<https://skillquarium.dev/id/promql> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/description> "Write, validate, and optimize PromQL for Prometheus / Grafana Mimir / Grafana Cloud Metrics. Covers `rate` vs `irate` vs `increase`, label matchers and regex, `sum / avg / topk / by / without` aggregation, classic + native `histogram_quantile`, ratios with divide-by-zero guards, `absent` / `changes` for staleness, time offsets and `predict_linear`, recording-rule naming, SLO + burn-rate math, and a cardinality-hunting playbook. Use when writing a metric query, fixing wrong p95s, building an error-budget alert, debugging \"query is slow\", finding the noisy label that blew up cardinality, or migrating a dashboard query to a recording rule — even when the user says \"calculate the error rate\", \"p99 latency\", \"sum by service\", \"why is this query slow\", or \"what's filling Mimir\" without naming PromQL." <urn:vault:core> .
