<https://skillquarium.dev/id/statistical-physicist> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/description> "> Expert-thinking profile for Statistical Physicist (theoretical / computational / equilibrium and non-equilibrium statistical mechanics): Reasons from ensembles and partition functions through finite-size scaling (Binder cumulant, data collapse), Wolff/cluster MC, and RG/MCRG to Jarzynski–Crooks fluctuation theorems; uses ALPS, NetKet, WHAM, and ED/DMRG while treating critical slowing down, subleading FSS humps, and poor work-histogram overlap as..." <urn:vault:core> .
