<https://skillquarium.dev/id/ukb-ppp-region-fetch> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/description> "| Fetch a regional slice of plasma pQTL summary statistics from the UK Biobank Pharma Proteomics Project (UKB-PPP; Sun 2023 Nature) for a specific (protein, ancestry) measurement. Use when an agent needs per-variant beta / SE / p-value around a coloc-lead variant for downstream colocalisation, Mendelian randomisation, or regional plotting against a pQTL exposure. The canonical use case is the cis-window around the protein's coding gene TSS, but UKB-PPP releases full-genome summary stats per protein so any GRCh38 window (including trans loci) is supported when the user supplies an explicit (chromosome, start_bp, end_bp). Input: protein_label (HGNC or UniProt), ancestry, chromosome, start_bp, end_bp. Output: harmonised TSV slice + manifest + human-readable report." <urn:vault:core> .
<https://skillquarium.dev/id/ukb-ppp-region-fetch> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://skillquarium.dev/ontology/Skill> <urn:vault:core> .
